# The thread sanitizer's known reports, for tests/run_all.py --tsan. Each
# entry is one known bug, still open, in the maintainer's known-bugs.md, or a
# race that is there by design. A bug's entries come out with the change
# that fixes it, and the sanitizer must then find nothing there. Anything not
# listed here fails CI.
#
# A race: entry names a function anywhere in either thread's stack, or a
# global variable; a race_top: entry names the function that makes one of
# the two accesses itself, at the top of its stack; ^ and $ make the match
# exact. Under each entry, "hides at most" gives how many reports it may hide
# in each test, about twice the most seen in 30 runs (the count varies with
# timing); tests/run_all.py fails a test in which an entry hides more, or any
# in a test its line doesn't name. Each group's comment names the
# release that is to fix its bug ("Fixed by b3."), checked at that release's
# step 4 (docs/release-checklist.md), or says it is there "By design";
# tests/run_all.py stops if one does neither.

# Known bug 20: the NV2A's registers are plain memory, which the game (in
# recomp_mmio_read and _write, src/kernel/kernel_mmio.c, and tests/nv2a_queue's
# DMA_GET poll) and the GPU thread (nv2a_ack_thread) read and write at once.
# The two race_top entries hide only a race in which the game's own access is
# made in those two functions, so a race below them on the register path
# (the APU's registers, the NV2A's interrupt registers, the pushbuffer flush)
# is still reported. Removed by the device register table
# (broader-fixes/CODEBASE.md R1). Fixed by b3.
race_top:^recomp_mmio_read$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 3
race_top:^recomp_mmio_write$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 16
race:^wait_get$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 4

# Known bug 20, and by design: the push buffer, in guest memory, written by
# the game and read by the GPU thread's walk. On the console DMA_PUT orders
# the two, and here it is plain memory (above). D3D also patches the buffer
# just ahead of DMA_GET while the walk may be reading it, as on the console.
# Fixed by b3, as far as known bug 20 goes; the patching is by design.
race:^nv2a_pb_scan$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 40000

# Known bug 20: the GPU thread's kick (s_kick_on, a switch cached lazily, and
# s_hurry), written by the game's thread and read by the GPU thread. Removed
# with the kick itself (CODEBASE.md R3) and the switch registry (R10).
# Fixed by b3.
race:^s_kick_on$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 8
race:^s_hurry$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 8

# Known bug 20: switches cached lazily by whichever thread reads them first:
# RECOMP_NV2A_QUEUE (nv2a_queue_on) and the software methods' mode
# (swm_mode). Removed by the switch registry (CODEBASE.md R10). Fixed by b3.
race:^nv2a_queue_on$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 6
race:^swm_mode$

# Known bug 20: the GPU queue's counts, kept by the GPU thread and read for
# the log by the game's thread. No change planned yet. Fixed by b3.
race:^nv2a_queue_report$
#   hides at most: nv2a_queue 8

# Known bug 25: the USB controller's registers (s_hc) are plain memory, read
# and written at once by the controller's thread and the game's USB driver
# (xbox_OhciWrite), the status and command words each with a read, a change
# and a write on both sides (tests/usb_interrupt). Removed by the device
# register table's USB part (broader-fixes/CODEBASE.md R1). Fixed by b3.
race:^s_hc$
#   hides at most: usb_interrupt 6

# By design: tests/fence_wait's fence word, in guest memory, written by the
# GPU side and polled by the game, as on the console.
race:^g_guest$
#   hides at most: fence_wait 4
